# The law rank/composition_closure.sqlc owes: under any fusion, the room to shift supply among the
# layers at the bottom without moving the figure at the top is the room inside each fusion below
# it, added up. One row.
#
# The identity
#   Inside one fusion, the room to shift supply among its parts without moving its figure is one
#   fewer than its parts. Nest fusions and the rooms add up. The whole composition comes to a single
#   figure, so its room is one fewer than the layers at the bottom, and the two routes are that and
#   the per-fusion rooms added over every fusion beneath the top.
#
# What it can catch, which is not the arithmetic
#   Where every layer is reached by one path, the identity is forced by counting, so what this law
#   really checks is that under each fusion every layer is reached by one path. A layer at the
#   bottom reached by a second path raises the per-fusion total and leaves the bottom count alone;
#   a loop takes layers off the bottom count without taking the fusions. Both land here, and this
#   law names the top fusion, which neither of the other checks does: checks/jagged_layer.sqlc
#   names the fusion whose own parts overlap, and algebra/cycle_space.sqlc reports one number for
#   the corpus.
#
# And the one way the top figure moves, in the same row
#   The whole composition comes to one figure, so `row_dim` is 1 at any depth, and every layer at
#   the bottom reaches the top through conversion factors whose product is positive, or that nobody
#   stated. Those two must cover every layer: a product of zero would need a factor of zero, which
#   `pm.part`'s own CHECK refuses, and a negative one is not a conversion. So nothing put into the
#   bottom layers is lost on the way up.
#
# It needs two levels to test anything
#   At one level the two routes are the same count, so a corpus of single-level compositions passes
#   this law having compared nothing. The floor requires a fusion whose composition reaches two
#   levels, which is where the sum over levels first has more than one term.
#
# Every fusion, not only the tops
#   rank/composition_closure.sqlc takes each fusion as the top of its own composition, so a defect
#   under an inner fusion is reported at that fusion and at every fusion above it. Both are true:
#   the identity fails for the inner fusion on its own, and for each one above because it contains
#   the inner one.
#
# Probe
#   examples/probes runs it as `composition_closure`. In a rolled-back transaction, give a fusion a
#   part naming a layer already reachable beneath it through another composition, and this law must
#   fail at that fusion and at nothing that does not contain it.
-- rank/composition_closure.sqlc: the whole composition's room against the sum of its levels'.
SELECT a.slug AS law, p.subject, p.holds, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(algebra/roster.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT 'rank/composition_closure' AS subject,
           count(*) > 0
           AND count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.deepest >= 2) > 0
           AND count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.closure_kernel <> c.sum_kernel) = 0
           AND count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.row_dim <> 1) = 0
           AND count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.leaves_positive + c.leaves_unknown <> c.leaves) = 0
                                                                                     AS holds,
           format('%s root(s), %s reaching two levels or more; %s whose own room is not that of '
                  'its fusions added up, %s with a leaf whose factors along the path multiply to '
                  'neither a positive number nor an unstated one, %s leaf arrival(s) unstated%s',
                  count(*), count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.deepest >= 2),
                  count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.closure_kernel <> c.sum_kernel),
                  count(*) FILTER (WHERE c.leaves_positive + c.leaves_unknown <> c.leaves),
                  coalesce(sum(c.leaves_unknown), 0),
                  coalesce(': ' || string_agg(format('%s/%s wants %s and sums to %s',
                                                     c.composition, c.composed_layer,
                                                     c.closure_kernel, c.sum_kernel),
                                              ', ' ORDER BY c.composition, c.composed_layer)
                                   FILTER (WHERE c.closure_kernel <> c.sum_kernel), ''))
                                                                                     AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(rank/composition_closure.sqlc)
    ) c
) p ON true
WHERE a.slug = 'composition_closure'
